1
00:00:00,015 --> 00:00:01,368
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,371 --> 00:00:02,948
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,641 --> 00:00:06,021
(Episode 25)

4
00:00:07,763 --> 00:00:08,891
Sa Bin.

5
00:00:10,584 --> 00:00:11,877
I...

6
00:00:12,908 --> 00:00:15,609
fell in love and had a daughter.

7
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:22,798
Because of her,
I took every insult and humiliation.

8
00:00:24,832 --> 00:00:26,869
Now she's pushing me away.

9
00:00:28,984 --> 00:00:30,744
I'm her mother.

10
00:00:31,645 --> 00:00:34,056
She's my whole reason for living.

11
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:39,887
No wonder you're drinking.

12
00:00:41,102 --> 00:00:42,373
Right?

13
00:00:45,695 --> 00:00:47,869
I knew you were a true friend, Sa Bin.

14
00:00:49,114 --> 00:00:50,310
Cheers.

15
00:01:03,342 --> 00:01:04,485
Thanks.

16
00:01:07,636 --> 00:01:08,994
Enjoy.

17
00:01:13,279 --> 00:01:14,279
You're here.

18
00:01:14,571 --> 00:01:16,390
Weren't you teaching the kids art tonight?

19
00:01:16,462 --> 00:01:19,072
Ji Ni couldn't make it,
so I filled in with a different class.

20
00:01:19,144 --> 00:01:22,552
- Why? What happened?
- Everything came out.

21
00:01:24,693 --> 00:01:27,204
- What's she going to do?
- It's a complete mess.

22
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:30,781
They say no secret stays hidden.

23
00:01:30,925 --> 00:01:32,817
She must be having a really hard time.

24
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:35,433
- She was terrified of her mom.
- Yeah.

25
00:01:35,758 --> 00:01:37,377
I want to go help,

26
00:01:37,379 --> 00:01:39,195
but I don't think I should get involved.

27
00:01:39,198 --> 00:01:40,765
So I'm staying out of it.

28
00:01:47,532 --> 00:01:50,375
- What brings you here?
- Do I need a reservation to come here?

29
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:52,844
An iced Americano. Five extra shots.

30
00:01:53,177 --> 00:01:55,321
- Trying to poison yourself?
- You don't sell it?

31
00:01:55,346 --> 00:01:56,626
Sure I do.

32
00:01:59,405 --> 00:02:01,627
- Can we talk?
- No.

33
00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:05,086
You'll just say something awful,
so I'm not talking to you.

34
00:02:05,089 --> 00:02:07,494
Even Do Do Hee has something
she's afraid of?

35
00:02:08,232 --> 00:02:10,502
Stay out of it. Just make the coffee.

36
00:02:10,523 --> 00:02:13,370
Yes, the customer is always right.

37
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:18,650
Thanks.

38
00:02:23,342 --> 00:02:25,725
- You're not going after her?
- She said no.

39
00:02:26,052 --> 00:02:28,083
Besides, I came to see Tae O.

40
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,527
You're pretty cold.

41
00:02:29,772 --> 00:02:31,717
Sometimes people need space.

42
00:02:38,627 --> 00:02:40,559
I guess it's not that passionate.

43
00:02:40,992 --> 00:02:42,533
Do Hee must be worried sick.

44
00:02:43,464 --> 00:02:44,644
Serves her right.

45
00:02:48,782 --> 00:02:50,070
Be careful.

46
00:02:50,592 --> 00:02:51,801
Hold on.

47
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,691
Just go.

48
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:58,588
I don't need anything. Just go.

49
00:02:59,051 --> 00:03:02,315
- Mom!
- Your mom's had a bit too much.

50
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:03,977
This way.

51
00:03:06,192 --> 00:03:07,586
Be careful.

52
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,497
- Here.
- Easy.

53
00:03:16,815 --> 00:03:18,382
- I'll cover her up.
- Okay.

54
00:03:23,051 --> 00:03:24,490
Get some rest.

55
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,090
Thank you.

56
00:03:33,624 --> 00:03:35,607
I don't know what to say to you.

57
00:03:36,912 --> 00:03:39,884
She kept mumbling about what happened,
so I don't know the details,

58
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,394
but she seems really upset.

59
00:03:43,371 --> 00:03:45,487
Yes. It's because of me.

60
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:46,980
I'm sure you have your reasons.

61
00:03:47,527 --> 00:03:48,530
But...

62
00:03:48,664 --> 00:03:51,834
Your mom just lost her husband,
so try to be understanding.

63
00:03:52,521 --> 00:03:54,246
I haven't been through it myself,

64
00:03:54,601 --> 00:03:58,370
but they say losing a spouse
can really affect your mental state.

65
00:03:58,373 --> 00:04:01,298
Especially since your mom and dad
were so close, right?

66
00:04:01,763 --> 00:04:03,723
Yes. I understand.

67
00:04:03,906 --> 00:04:07,321
- See you later. I'll get going.
- Okay. Take care.

68
00:04:30,041 --> 00:04:33,691
Mom!

69
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,580
I don't want to. Get out.

70
00:04:39,468 --> 00:04:41,064
I'm going to die.

71
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:45,464
This miserable life!
It'll all be over if I die.

72
00:04:51,919 --> 00:04:53,971
I can't do this anymore.

73
00:04:54,495 --> 00:04:56,838
It's too hard.

74
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,669
I'm going to die.

75
00:05:01,690 --> 00:05:07,750
- I'm going to die.
- Mom, I'm sorry.

76
00:05:15,948 --> 00:05:21,076
I'm so sorry, Mom.

77
00:05:48,169 --> 00:05:49,840
What are you doing up this early?

78
00:05:52,554 --> 00:05:54,721
I need to help Ji Ni.

79
00:05:55,212 --> 00:05:57,709
- I'm going to send gifts first.
- "Gifts?"

80
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,558
Meat, fruit, wine, cheese, fish,

81
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,088
and Vietnamese food. All of this?

82
00:06:04,091 --> 00:06:05,896
Should I add some jewelry too?

83
00:06:05,998 --> 00:06:08,323
- Or maybe cash?
- That's illegal.

84
00:06:08,472 --> 00:06:10,907
The doctor already warned us
to be careful about that.

85
00:06:11,832 --> 00:06:15,955
So I'm writing something like this,
but it feels too insignificant.

86
00:06:17,232 --> 00:06:21,921
Anyway, since this pain in the neck
said she'd calm down,

87
00:06:22,327 --> 00:06:25,388
we'll send the gifts first,
then go apologize in person.

88
00:06:25,796 --> 00:06:26,967
Who said that?

89
00:06:27,070 --> 00:06:28,729
You really know a lot of weird things.

90
00:06:28,731 --> 00:06:30,213
My dad told me.

91
00:06:30,933 --> 00:06:32,429
We need to help Ji Ni.

92
00:06:32,432 --> 00:06:34,998
It's too sad to leave her to face
this alone.

93
00:06:35,724 --> 00:06:38,780
My wife's pretty admirable. You're loyal.

94
00:06:39,137 --> 00:06:40,559
I'm going there today too.

95
00:06:41,173 --> 00:06:43,640
I'll get down on my knees
and beg for forgiveness.

96
00:06:43,666 --> 00:06:45,473
She saved O Reum's life.

97
00:06:52,717 --> 00:06:54,871
Your coffee is ready. Enjoy.

98
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:59,203
These days, they're even cutting
established producers.

99
00:06:59,292 --> 00:07:00,481
What were you thinking,

100
00:07:00,483 --> 00:07:03,773
quitting your job
over some impossible romance?

101
00:07:04,457 --> 00:07:06,675
I can't help it. That's just who I am.

102
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,573
Want to work with me?

103
00:07:09,211 --> 00:07:11,489
Did you start your own company?

104
00:07:11,558 --> 00:07:12,640
I'm planning to.

105
00:07:13,283 --> 00:07:16,123
Doing the same thing every day
gets boring, doesn't it?

106
00:07:17,532 --> 00:07:19,146
You're even more reckless than me.

107
00:07:19,733 --> 00:07:20,940
Actually,

108
00:07:22,281 --> 00:07:25,125
I have an investor who wants me
to make a dating show.

109
00:07:25,245 --> 00:07:26,845
I thought of you.

110
00:07:26,963 --> 00:07:29,165
But I'm a documentary person.

111
00:07:29,266 --> 00:07:32,092
- I can't do variety shows.
- You know Shin Jung Woo, right?

112
00:07:34,175 --> 00:07:36,738
- Him too?
- Exactly.

113
00:07:37,148 --> 00:07:38,398
Just follow us.

114
00:07:38,472 --> 00:07:39,732
Decide by this week.

115
00:07:39,770 --> 00:07:43,321
Once you decide, I'll share the concept.
It's really fun.

116
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:45,014
Variety shows are the future.

117
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,460
Looks like it's true.

118
00:07:51,817 --> 00:07:54,091
- Wait a second.
- Sure.

119
00:08:00,664 --> 00:08:01,944
Excuse me...

120
00:08:05,470 --> 00:08:07,090
Were you okay yesterday?

121
00:08:08,024 --> 00:08:09,757
Is that why you came?

122
00:08:10,212 --> 00:08:12,257
I figured it might not be a good idea
for me to contact you directly,

123
00:08:12,612 --> 00:08:14,390
so I set up a meeting here at the café...

124
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:18,087
- to see if we might run into each other.
- I'm fine. Don't worry.

125
00:08:18,738 --> 00:08:21,366
I was worried
you might've run away from home.

126
00:08:21,550 --> 00:08:24,744
If you had, I was going to help you
find a place to stay.

127
00:08:28,392 --> 00:08:29,971
I was trying to make you laugh.

128
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:37,367
It's not that serious.
But thank you for your concern.

129
00:08:40,932 --> 00:08:42,467
Then take care.

130
00:08:42,984 --> 00:08:46,377
If you ever need help, call me. Anytime.

131
00:08:47,165 --> 00:08:48,302
Okay.

132
00:08:55,236 --> 00:08:57,107
Wasn't that the same guy from last time?

133
00:08:57,972 --> 00:08:59,565
The one who called you a "jerk."

134
00:09:00,735 --> 00:09:01,742
Yeah.

135
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,492
He's gotten really polite.

136
00:09:05,190 --> 00:09:06,546
Because of O Reum?

137
00:09:07,342 --> 00:09:08,634
Probably.

138
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:16,021
Seeing him today,
he's actually really handsome.

139
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:17,952
What's with you?

140
00:09:18,897 --> 00:09:20,018
Hey, it's just...

141
00:09:20,032 --> 00:09:21,850
I'm just saying, can't I say that?

142
00:09:22,247 --> 00:09:24,379
Then go tell him yourself.

143
00:09:25,144 --> 00:09:27,355
I wish he'd come to the café more often.

144
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:29,514
Cute.

145
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:32,290
If he liked Han Jeong Won,

146
00:09:32,315 --> 00:09:34,327
- then I'm probably not his type, right?
- Who knows?

147
00:09:34,457 --> 00:09:36,387
If he got tired of that type,

148
00:09:36,389 --> 00:09:38,821
he might switch to someone like you,
cute and bubbly.

149
00:09:38,824 --> 00:09:40,942
Hey, don't give me hope.

150
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:42,459
It makes me start expecting things.

151
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:48,407
- You're here?
- Hello.

152
00:09:48,529 --> 00:09:51,085
Come on in, my little ones.

153
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:53,232
Let's check your homework first. Sit down.

154
00:09:55,321 --> 00:09:56,627
Ta-da.

155
00:09:56,815 --> 00:09:59,935
What was on your mind
when you drew this face?

156
00:10:00,003 --> 00:10:01,725
I just drew it.

157
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:04,929
Then let's think about it.

158
00:10:05,754 --> 00:10:08,957
What were you doing
before you made this face?

159
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:13,670
I think you fought with a friend
and you're upset.

160
00:10:13,725 --> 00:10:14,948
That's right.

161
00:10:15,624 --> 00:10:17,262
So this isn't your friend,
this is you, right?

162
00:10:17,342 --> 00:10:18,540
This is your face?

163
00:10:20,212 --> 00:10:21,752
How did you know?

164
00:10:22,087 --> 00:10:23,377
I just know.

165
00:10:23,931 --> 00:10:25,241
Then...

166
00:10:26,232 --> 00:10:29,011
how about we say you're angry
because paint splashed on your face?

167
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:32,648
Your assignment was to draw a portrait
with a story, right?

168
00:10:33,097 --> 00:10:36,946
Let's add a big splash of red paint here.

169
00:10:37,282 --> 00:10:38,440
Should we?

170
00:10:41,805 --> 00:10:42,942
You try it.

171
00:10:43,262 --> 00:10:44,478
Should we try?

172
00:10:48,502 --> 00:10:50,061
I'm completely drained.

173
00:10:50,070 --> 00:10:52,282
I feel like I'm going to die
trying to earn just a little extra money.

174
00:10:53,796 --> 00:10:55,373
This is so exhausting.

175
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:57,448
Were we like this when we were kids?

176
00:10:58,015 --> 00:10:59,867
How do they never stop even for a second?

177
00:11:01,518 --> 00:11:03,082
I'm starving. What should we eat?

178
00:11:03,291 --> 00:11:04,948
I don't even have the energy
to lift a spoon.

179
00:11:06,972 --> 00:11:08,834
Do you think this is enough
of a transfusion?

180
00:11:09,618 --> 00:11:10,904
How did you know to come?

181
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:13,140
You asked me for help.

182
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:14,281
You don't remember?

183
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:18,267
- I was just saying that.
- Hey.

184
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:20,194
And here I was actually believing you.

185
00:11:21,748 --> 00:11:22,848
Go ahead, eat.

186
00:11:24,891 --> 00:11:26,044
Thank you.

187
00:11:26,065 --> 00:11:28,560
- You must've had a rough time.
- Don't even get me started.

188
00:11:29,004 --> 00:11:32,095
But if you're out, what about your work
at the Art and Culture Center?

189
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:34,044
I do my job at night.

190
00:11:35,851 --> 00:11:37,250
At night?

191
00:11:37,253 --> 00:11:39,205
What are you thinking?

192
00:11:39,972 --> 00:11:42,465
I stay up all night talking
to performers in Europe.

193
00:11:43,961 --> 00:11:45,679
We're preparing the center's fall, winter,

194
00:11:45,681 --> 00:11:47,767
and next spring programs.

195
00:11:48,312 --> 00:11:51,127
Orchestra tours to Korea, solo recitals,
all sorts of things.

196
00:11:51,224 --> 00:11:52,474
You speak German too?

197
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:59,038
Hello, this is Im Ji Hu, director
of the Korea Art and Culture Center.

198
00:11:59,098 --> 00:12:01,465
I'd like to inquire
about your performance schedule.

199
00:12:03,295 --> 00:12:05,575
I send emails, make calls,
things like that.

200
00:12:05,653 --> 00:12:06,688
Eat before it gets cold.

201
00:12:08,877 --> 00:12:12,102
- You speak so many languages. Impressive.
- Well, I studied abroad.

202
00:12:20,222 --> 00:12:21,544
This drawing is really good.

203
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:25,667
Her mother wants her to attend
an arts school.

204
00:12:25,992 --> 00:12:27,809
But the kid herself
hasn't really thought about it yet.

205
00:12:28,782 --> 00:12:30,127
I heard your mom found out.

206
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:36,063
- Jung A must've told you.
- That must've been hard.

207
00:12:37,022 --> 00:12:39,040
I think it'll be hard for a while.

208
00:12:39,190 --> 00:12:41,475
Wounds from family tend to last.

209
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:43,034
You should take good care of her.

210
00:12:43,212 --> 00:12:45,136
It hasn't been long since your dad passed.

211
00:12:46,095 --> 00:12:47,312
That's right.

212
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:51,661
But how do you know all this so well?

213
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:54,029
Life is pretty much the same for everyone.

214
00:12:55,022 --> 00:12:56,590
Is there anything I can help you with?

215
00:12:57,304 --> 00:12:59,175
You've already helped me a lot.

216
00:13:01,354 --> 00:13:03,904
- I should go to the publishing company.
- I'll come with you.

217
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,954
The writer I'm trying to contact
lives near the publishing complex,

218
00:13:05,956 --> 00:13:06,996
so I was heading that way.

219
00:13:07,705 --> 00:13:09,712
Okay, thank you.

220
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:22,073
What do you do when a painting
doesn't turn out the way you imagined?

221
00:13:24,567 --> 00:13:26,257
I just think maybe it's not my painting.

222
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:30,969
- That's kind of cool.
- I'm good at letting go.

223
00:13:30,972 --> 00:13:33,852
- If it's not mine, I drop it right away.
- I'd like to learn...

224
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:35,379
that attitude too.

225
00:13:35,737 --> 00:13:38,367
- I tend to hold on too much.
- It's not easy.

226
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,621
I paid a lot of "tuition"
in life to learn it.

227
00:13:43,692 --> 00:13:46,571
Lately, things have been a bit difficult
between me and Do Hee.

228
00:13:47,308 --> 00:13:48,504
You know that, right?

229
00:13:48,610 --> 00:13:51,460
I'm sure Jung A didn't only tell me
about you.

230
00:13:52,634 --> 00:13:54,954
I've heard some things, yeah.

231
00:13:55,274 --> 00:13:58,473
My first project at the center
didn't go well, so I was upset,

232
00:13:58,710 --> 00:14:01,775
but I think I got even angrier
because people noticed how I felt.

233
00:14:02,110 --> 00:14:04,975
- That happens.
- That's why I asked...

234
00:14:05,292 --> 00:14:07,821
what do you do when a painting
doesn't turn out as imagined.

235
00:14:13,632 --> 00:14:15,502
When you make that expression,

236
00:14:15,504 --> 00:14:17,777
you don't look like you're in your 20s,
you look like you're in your 40s.

237
00:14:19,992 --> 00:14:22,027
Honestly, I wish I were in my 40s.

238
00:14:23,138 --> 00:14:24,138
What?

239
00:14:49,261 --> 00:14:50,261
Yes.

240
00:14:55,898 --> 00:14:58,439
CEO Na, the investment approval
document has arrived.

241
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,865
- Really?
- I saw you completed the transfer.

242
00:15:03,379 --> 00:15:06,063
Of course. You did it too, right?

243
00:15:06,065 --> 00:15:07,065
Of course.

244
00:15:07,276 --> 00:15:10,812
Just stamp it with the company seal,
and it'll be finalized.

245
00:15:11,826 --> 00:15:12,826
Okay.

246
00:15:18,565 --> 00:15:20,688
It goes to the children
as inheritance, right?

247
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:21,690
Of course.

248
00:15:27,814 --> 00:15:30,022
I've really gone all in,

249
00:15:31,148 --> 00:15:32,356
but now I'm getting nervous.

250
00:15:32,897 --> 00:15:34,771
You know I even took out
a loan on my house.

251
00:15:34,773 --> 00:15:36,188
This has to work.

252
00:15:36,190 --> 00:15:37,562
Don't worry.

253
00:15:37,565 --> 00:15:39,231
K-culture is taking the world by storm.

254
00:15:39,345 --> 00:15:40,550
This is the perfect time.

255
00:15:41,356 --> 00:15:42,356
Yes.

256
00:15:44,523 --> 00:15:46,356
(Na Se Ri)

257
00:15:47,565 --> 00:15:48,565
Here you go.

258
00:15:48,863 --> 00:15:51,342
I'll take care of it and report back.

259
00:15:52,190 --> 00:15:53,190
Okay.

260
00:16:01,981 --> 00:16:05,023
Honey, I did the right thing, right?

261
00:16:05,815 --> 00:16:07,823
I even took out a mortgage on the house.

262
00:16:12,148 --> 00:16:13,148
Yes.

263
00:16:16,356 --> 00:16:18,038
Why do you keep doing this?

264
00:16:18,378 --> 00:16:20,731
You took turns pressuring Ji Ni
like this too, didn't you?

265
00:16:20,773 --> 00:16:22,729
No. I really didn't know.

266
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:24,100
Who would believe that?

267
00:16:25,023 --> 00:16:26,606
I begged my mom...

268
00:16:27,304 --> 00:16:29,929
- to apologize and ask for permission.
- What?

269
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:31,780
I knew it was a terrible thing
to do to her, but I still did it.

270
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:33,418
I begged her so relentlessly...

271
00:16:33,773 --> 00:16:36,523
that my brother told me
I could have another child.

272
00:16:36,858 --> 00:16:38,789
I couldn't stand seeing my child suffer.

273
00:16:39,438 --> 00:16:41,447
And now he's alive. Good for you.

274
00:16:42,606 --> 00:16:46,453
Thanks to you, he got a second chance.

275
00:16:50,398 --> 00:16:52,065
Thank you so much.

276
00:16:53,106 --> 00:16:55,523
I will never forget what you did for us.

277
00:16:55,891 --> 00:16:57,637
I'm sorry for frightening you,

278
00:16:58,315 --> 00:17:00,648
and for deceiving you.

279
00:17:01,362 --> 00:17:02,570
Please forgive me.

280
00:17:02,867 --> 00:17:04,581
Enough. Get up.

281
00:17:04,981 --> 00:17:06,940
You're always getting on your knees.

282
00:17:07,065 --> 00:17:08,440
Please forgive me.

283
00:17:09,199 --> 00:17:10,703
If you can forgive me,

284
00:17:11,190 --> 00:17:13,311
I'll do anything to show my gratitude.

285
00:17:14,023 --> 00:17:15,356
"Anything?"

286
00:17:17,038 --> 00:17:19,038
Then give me the Seo Chon house.

287
00:17:20,815 --> 00:17:23,246
- What?
- I said give me the Seo Chon house.

288
00:17:23,906 --> 00:17:25,565
You came here before to take our house.

289
00:17:25,606 --> 00:17:26,981
You took Ji Ni's bone marrow,

290
00:17:27,023 --> 00:17:29,398
and thought you'd make up for it
with meat and drinks?

291
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:32,065
Or were you just going to give me
some money and leave?

292
00:17:32,148 --> 00:17:35,771
That house was a gift
from grandfather to mother.

293
00:17:35,773 --> 00:17:38,437
Can't you give it to me? Then leave.

294
00:17:38,581 --> 00:17:40,953
Begging here won't change anything.

295
00:17:41,570 --> 00:17:44,093
Don't come here and stir up my feelings.
Just go.

296
00:17:44,106 --> 00:17:45,315
Go.

297
00:18:37,812 --> 00:18:40,148
I'm barely holding on.

298
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,856
I'll get revenge after I die!

299
00:18:43,898 --> 00:18:45,815
Please just stop.

300
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:47,854
I'm the one who wants to die!

301
00:18:47,856 --> 00:18:49,898
I've done everything you wanted
my whole life.

302
00:18:51,981 --> 00:18:55,607
I can't let you be sad.

303
00:19:03,231 --> 00:19:04,940
(No Yeong Ju)

304
00:19:14,523 --> 00:19:16,270
Your daughter won't be able
to show her face in public either.

305
00:19:16,273 --> 00:19:17,648
I'll make sure they turn on her too.

306
00:19:29,898 --> 00:19:31,301
My sweet daughter.

307
00:19:31,635 --> 00:19:33,586
I don't blame you.

308
00:19:35,423 --> 00:19:37,077
You did the right thing.

309
00:20:03,606 --> 00:20:06,736
I invested a lot in the company
your dad left behind.

310
00:20:08,148 --> 00:20:10,848
You won't have to worry about living.

311
00:20:12,815 --> 00:20:14,226
I'll say it again.

312
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,069
I don't blame you at all.

313
00:20:18,742 --> 00:20:21,742
I'm just tired.

314
00:20:24,398 --> 00:20:25,950
I miss your dad.

315
00:20:27,273 --> 00:20:30,639
I just want to be with him again.

316
00:20:34,648 --> 00:20:36,945
- You're pretty.
- Ji Ni, look here.

317
00:20:36,981 --> 00:20:39,315
- Here.
- Here, Ji Ni.

318
00:20:39,356 --> 00:20:41,229
You're pretty.

319
00:20:41,231 --> 00:20:42,481
Here you go.

320
00:20:49,523 --> 00:20:50,667
Ji Ni.

321
00:20:51,231 --> 00:20:52,343
My daughter.

322
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:56,065
You suffered so much
because you had me as your mother.

323
00:20:57,981 --> 00:20:59,190
I'm sorry.

324
00:21:32,065 --> 00:21:33,271
Mom,

325
00:21:33,273 --> 00:21:37,145
why can't I call you Mom outside?

326
00:21:42,065 --> 00:21:43,701
I'm sorry, Ji Ni.

327
00:21:44,731 --> 00:21:46,311
I'm so sorry.

328
00:22:10,565 --> 00:22:12,490
The gastric lavage is complete.

329
00:22:13,690 --> 00:22:15,648
Is the guardian still not here?

330
00:22:15,690 --> 00:22:18,148
No, I still can't reach her.

331
00:22:19,315 --> 00:22:20,523
Please keep monitoring her.

332
00:22:20,606 --> 00:22:23,398
Excuse me. She'll be okay, right?

333
00:22:24,154 --> 00:22:25,779
There was a suicide note.

334
00:22:25,878 --> 00:22:26,896
Is she going to be okay?

335
00:22:26,898 --> 00:22:28,652
She took medication with alcohol.

336
00:22:30,273 --> 00:22:32,065
For now, all we can do is keep watching.

337
00:22:50,023 --> 00:22:52,690
How could you do this
when you have a child?

338
00:22:55,690 --> 00:22:58,190
Mom, what happened?

339
00:23:02,731 --> 00:23:03,940
My goodness...

340
00:23:05,356 --> 00:23:06,569
This can't be real.

341
00:23:06,731 --> 00:23:09,065
- How could she...
- I know.

342
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:23,481
I'm angry, but I also understand.

343
00:23:25,731 --> 00:23:27,870
She must've felt betrayed by Ji Ni.

344
00:23:28,190 --> 00:23:29,398
I get it.

345
00:23:29,898 --> 00:23:31,315
But does that justify something
this reckless?

346
00:23:31,356 --> 00:23:32,565
She's a mother.

347
00:23:33,356 --> 00:23:35,503
Being a mother
doesn't make you unbreakable.

348
00:23:35,648 --> 00:23:38,323
A single word or action from your child...

349
00:23:38,466 --> 00:23:39,856
can cut you to the bone.

350
00:23:40,815 --> 00:23:42,479
- Mom...
- That's enough.

351
00:23:42,523 --> 00:23:44,356
Try calling Ji Ni.

352
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,398
She's not answering at all.

353
00:23:46,731 --> 00:23:48,315
How did you find her?

354
00:23:48,690 --> 00:23:50,356
I wanted to drop off some soy milk broth,

355
00:23:50,481 --> 00:23:52,126
so I got the door code.

356
00:23:52,565 --> 00:23:55,973
And as I was leaving,
I heard music coming from the bedroom,

357
00:23:56,231 --> 00:23:57,981
so I went in and found her.

358
00:23:58,065 --> 00:23:59,361
It was almost a disaster.

359
00:24:02,523 --> 00:24:04,723
She's not picking up.
I'll leave a message.

360
00:24:14,148 --> 00:24:15,648
It's interesting, but...

361
00:24:16,648 --> 00:24:18,273
The situation feels too predictable.

362
00:24:18,398 --> 00:24:19,856
The king's son becomes king.

363
00:24:19,898 --> 00:24:22,842
No wonder our generation keeps talking
about "silver spoon" privilege.

364
00:24:23,106 --> 00:24:25,986
I think we need a different perspective.

365
00:24:26,273 --> 00:24:27,301
Yeah.

366
00:24:29,690 --> 00:24:31,412
- What is it?
- It's my mom...

367
00:24:31,648 --> 00:24:33,570
- My mom...
- What about your mom?

368
00:24:34,115 --> 00:24:35,259
I have to go.

369
00:24:35,261 --> 00:24:37,249
I'm sorry I can't help you finish.

370
00:24:37,266 --> 00:24:38,379
Want me to drive you?

371
00:24:39,006 --> 00:24:41,603
It's rush hour,
but we can take a back road.

372
00:24:41,606 --> 00:24:43,592
- Then I'd really appreciate it.
- Let's go.

373
00:24:58,773 --> 00:24:59,981
Mom.

374
00:25:00,065 --> 00:25:01,206
Mom!

375
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,745
Mom, can you hear me?

376
00:25:16,481 --> 00:25:17,690
Can you see me?

377
00:25:20,606 --> 00:25:22,408
If I can see Yeong Ju,

378
00:25:22,856 --> 00:25:24,484
I guess I'm still in hell.

379
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:25,830
Se Ri.

380
00:25:30,690 --> 00:25:31,770
Water, please.

381
00:25:31,773 --> 00:25:33,065
Yeah, water.

382
00:25:56,273 --> 00:25:59,273
Next time, take more pills.

383
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:02,490
Or try something more direct, as I did.

384
00:26:02,837 --> 00:26:03,921
Ji Ni.

385
00:26:03,924 --> 00:26:06,549
That's enough.
You can't say that to your mom.

386
00:26:09,690 --> 00:26:12,200
How can you live your whole life
thinking only of yourself?

387
00:26:13,527 --> 00:26:15,110
You gave birth to me on your own terms,

388
00:26:15,731 --> 00:26:17,856
and then wouldn't even let me
call you "Mom."

389
00:26:18,648 --> 00:26:20,709
You told me to toughen up
and be stronger,

390
00:26:20,981 --> 00:26:22,271
and this is all you've got?

391
00:26:23,023 --> 00:26:25,779
If you leave like this,
how am I supposed to live?

392
00:26:26,513 --> 00:26:29,371
How can a mother be this irresponsible?

393
00:26:29,481 --> 00:26:31,311
I did my best.

394
00:26:32,273 --> 00:26:36,065
I have nothing left to give,
and no strength left to keep going.

395
00:26:36,898 --> 00:26:38,680
I just want to follow your dad.

396
00:26:39,773 --> 00:26:41,398
You'll be fine without me anyway.

397
00:26:41,523 --> 00:26:42,606
Mom.

398
00:26:42,648 --> 00:26:45,148
I hate everything.
Everything feels like a burden.

399
00:26:45,231 --> 00:26:46,356
Don't say anything.

400
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:49,148
How can a mother say something like
that to her child?

401
00:26:50,523 --> 00:26:52,643
Get out. You're no better.

402
00:26:52,731 --> 00:26:54,625
Who treats their mother like this?

403
00:26:56,856 --> 00:26:58,218
People can hear everything outside.

404
00:26:58,398 --> 00:26:59,648
What is wrong with all of you?

405
00:27:00,065 --> 00:27:03,065
Are you going to give me Seo Chon?

406
00:27:03,148 --> 00:27:04,564
Have you thought about it?

407
00:27:06,356 --> 00:27:07,959
Seo Chon?

408
00:27:08,981 --> 00:27:10,429
Give me your house,

409
00:27:10,981 --> 00:27:12,727
if you're really grateful to me.

410
00:27:16,898 --> 00:27:19,894
What have you ever lost?

411
00:27:20,555 --> 00:27:21,894
You have everything.

412
00:27:22,648 --> 00:27:26,356
The documents, two sons, a house.

413
00:27:27,940 --> 00:27:29,893
I only have one daughter...

414
00:27:30,481 --> 00:27:32,550
and you didn't even let her go
to high school,

415
00:27:32,690 --> 00:27:34,690
and in the end,
you even took her bone marrow.

416
00:27:34,731 --> 00:27:36,580
Mom, please!

417
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:40,315
I can't forgive you.

418
00:27:41,565 --> 00:27:43,315
That's why I tried to die.

419
00:27:44,773 --> 00:27:46,856
Because no one is on my side.

420
00:28:10,940 --> 00:28:14,271
(Family Register)

421
00:28:14,273 --> 00:28:15,565
She's playing the victim,

422
00:28:15,606 --> 00:28:16,815
when she's the one who caused it.

423
00:28:16,898 --> 00:28:18,479
There's a limit to acting spoiled.

424
00:28:18,481 --> 00:28:20,940
At her age,
throwing tantrums like that is ridiculous.

425
00:28:21,190 --> 00:28:22,604
Watch what you're doing.

426
00:28:22,606 --> 00:28:24,896
How dare you swing your handbag
in front of me?

427
00:28:24,898 --> 00:28:26,646
Father, please help me.

428
00:28:26,648 --> 00:28:28,815
How am I supposed to live
with someone like you?

429
00:28:28,898 --> 00:28:30,396
Then come live with me.

430
00:28:30,398 --> 00:28:32,523
What is wrong with you? It's not like
there's a husband to steal anyway.

431
00:28:32,648 --> 00:28:35,190
I seriously don't understand you.

432
00:28:36,095 --> 00:28:38,095
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
